From: Stained Glass OS <dev@stained-glass.example>
Subject: shell32: the Desktop namespace has no "/"

The Desktop's shell namespace -- what a file dialog's "Desktop" shows -- listed
"/", Wine's view of the Unix file system, which Windows does not have. It is
no longer registered there; the Unix root stays a drive under This PC and
a Unix path typed into a dialog still opens. Existing prefixes drop the key
through sg-shell's defaults. Gate: make test-nsroot.
---
--- a/dlls/shell32/shell32.rgs
+++ b/dlls/shell32/shell32.rgs
@@ -33,7 +33,6 @@
                             {
                                 '{450D8FBA-AD25-11D0-98A8-0800361B1103}' = s 'My Documents'
                                 '{645FF040-5081-101B-9F08-00AA002F954E}' = s 'Trash'
-                                '{9D20AAE8-0625-44B0-9CA7-71889C2254D9}' = s '/'
                             }
                         }
                         NoRemove MyComputer
